WEBVTT

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:07.460
There's something inside that crystal… a flame?

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.250
This year's practical exercise is all about mana provision!

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:17.330
This giant crystal can measure
the amount and quality of your mana!

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.960
But don't think it's just a boring old measurement device!

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:24.880
We're testing your ability to supply mana
to an entity through a physical barrier

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.630
by having you supply mana through the crystal
to this amorphous flame!

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.670
As such, you'll pour as much mana
as you can into the contained flame!

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:35.710
The amount you're able to provide
will determine your score!

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.750
W-wow.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.670
That sounds kinda easy.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.380
So we just need to fill the crystal with mana, right?

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:45.210
All right, let's start with Student #1!

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:54.000
No... there's no way this is going to be THAT easy.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:18.540
Shiro ka kuro kongaragatte gray

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:21.750
Itsudatte aimai na mama de

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:27.750
Tayorinaku aruku tonari de hohoenderu kimi

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:31.210
Akogare wa tashika da toshite

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:34.420
Hateshinaku tooku mabushii

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:40.210
Chippokena kono genjou Abracada-Boo mahou kakete yo

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:46.420
Kimi no hitomi no yami ni kakushita

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:53.080
Samishisa wa yasashii uta de dakishimeteitai no ni

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:57.790
Sekaijuu ga uso datte sawagihajimetatte

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:00.540
Kimi ga kimi naraba

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:06.790
Kirameku kaze o makiokoshi shinjitsu o sakebu

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:10.420
Sekaijuu ga tsumi datte togameta toshitatte

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:13.130
Tatta hitori demo

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:16.290
Kimi o rikai shi tsuzuketai

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:21.790
I'm on your side mamotte ageru

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:30.920
<b>THE MAGE OF HEAVEN'S WILL</b>

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:39.920
Dammit! Come on!

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:42.830
I'm giving it all I've got!

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:43.750
Next number!

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.500
GO!

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:00.380
Next number!

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:08.040
Next number!

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.290
Seems most are having a rough time.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.830
Yeah. It'll be less than 10% at this rate…

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:21.750
They're failing because they assumed it'd be easy!
The proctor even warned them!

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.420
Next number, #87!

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:29.580
Watch this.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:36.710
I know the trick to this test.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:43.380
We're funneling mana into the flame, not the crystal.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:47.920
Crystal is a mineral formation that excels at storing mana.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.670
Pouring mana into it won't mean
the mana will make it to the center!

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:57.290
I'm going to give it all I have! Support me, Sylphide!

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:04.380
I just need to focus on the flame in the center!

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:08.540
If I get distracted, the mana will flow
into the crystal instead…

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:13.630
But controlling my mana that precisely
is a piece of cake for me!

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:23.080
Not bad. You're certainly the top scorer so far.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:24.790
Yes!

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.250
Easy as pie!

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:31.880
I knew you'd do it, Lilia!

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:32.880
Next!

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:37.330
Sheesh, you don't need to go to Ortigia to ace this test.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.000
Watch real close, now!

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:45.580
What's with him?

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:48.830
Seems he's a student at another school.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:55.630
Wow, not bad.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:57.500
Yeah.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:00.540
We can't let ourselves be outdone.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:01.460
Absolutely!

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:29.920
Ortigia's students certainly live up
to their institution's reputation.

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:33.380
Though this one only barely scraped by.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:34.830
I suppose.

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:38.540
Great job!

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:39.540
T'was easy!

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:46.670
But if this is all Ortigia has for us this year,
I'll be disappointed.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:50.580
All right, last one, #108!

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:52.580
Y-yes sir!

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.130
Why are two people going up?

00:05:58.130 --> 00:05:59.580
Who is that girl?

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:00.170
She's huge!

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:01.130
THEY'RE huge…

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:07.500
What, did you bring your mommy with you?
What is this, preschool?

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:11.790
E-excuse me, only test takers and staff are allowed to-

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:13.130
No, they're fine.

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:13.710
Huh?

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:20.040
I got a note about this from Ortigia. She's his familiar.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:20.830
What?!

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.830
A human familiar…

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:27.750
I've proctored this test for a long time,
and I've never seen nor heard of such a thing.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:31.080
And she's ginormous…

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:36.130
It's much bigger up close.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:37.420
Yeah.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:39.380
I knew it.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:40.710
Knew what?

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:44.630
Oh, when I was looking at it from far away,
I had a feeling…

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:52.960
It's just as I thought. This is no ordinary crystal.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.790
The crystal itself is acting as a pseudomatrix of formulae.

00:06:57.630 --> 00:07:05.750
The construction itself is simple, but it's enough
to guide mana along its path and out of the crystal.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:07.290
However...

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.830
Why's Alto going around it?

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:14.830
Here!

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:19.380
Right here is where the formula
creates a straight line into the center!

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:27.290
Excuse me, um, do we have to do it in front?

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:31.170
No, you can apply mana from wherever you like.

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:36.920
He caught on to the real test being performed here:

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:41.040
measuring your ability to decipher
and understand magic formulae.

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:47.290
That crystal is a specially-made mana conduit.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:52.920
The location you choose to supply mana from
greatly determines your success.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:53.130
<b>Average</b>

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:53.130
<b>Somewhat Weak</b>

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:53.130
<b>Weak</b>

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:53.130
<b>Strong</b>

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:59.290
And of those potential locations,
the best spot to supply mana is from the back!

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:05.540
Unless you have sufficient knowledge
and a keen eye for magical formulae,

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:07.920
you won't be able to find that spot!

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:15.330
I'm glad we've got someone who's a little better
than the rest. He definitely passes.

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:17.630
Alto.

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.960
That's not the right spot, is it?

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:27.420
You're right. That's not it.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.460
Whoa, whoa, not that!

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:37.330
I promised you…

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:42.130
...I'd get stronger!

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:57.130
What?! It's huge! And the flames have turned silver?!

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:01.750
Impossible! That's the most difficult spot to supply mana!

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:05.630
He chose that spot intentionally?!

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:12.750
Incredible… This feels like nothing…

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:17.540
…not compared to how crazy difficult
supplying mana to Vermeil has been!

00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:26.210
This crystal might be thick and tough to get through,
but it's nothing compared to the contract with Vermeil!

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:35.330
He can supply even more?!

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:38.750
Alto.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:47.880
Don't hold back. Scare the hell out of all of them.

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:48.830
All right!

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:10.380
Huh?

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:39.330
I-I-I-I... I-I'm...

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:42.500
I'M SO SORRY!

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:47.170
I'm sorry! I'm so, so sorry!

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:52.170
I, uh, I didn't mean to break it, I swear!

00:10:52.170 --> 00:11:00.000
Um, I'm sorry! I really am! I'm really REALLY sorry! Really!

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:56.540
I can't believe the crystal shattered…

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:04.500
So, uh, does this mean…

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:08.210
...I don't pass?

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:13.920
Don't be ridiculous. You pass with flying colors.

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:18.170
Sir! They're supposed to find that out later!

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:21.080
How am I supposed to tell him
that he didn't pass after THAT?

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:28.250
Of course, you only pass this practical exam.
Do poorly on the written and you'll flunk.

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:29.830
So don't get cocky.

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:31.420
Y-yes sir!

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:33.290
If you're done, then get outta here.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:37.710
Thank you, sir!

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:41.170
Sorry!

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:41.960
That was wild!

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:42.420
I'm so glad...

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:48.420
I still can't believe this happened.

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:51.420
Could the crystal have been defective?

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:53.080
Not a chance.

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:59.630
I'm surprised someone could even shatter the crystal.

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:07.290
A Gold Square couldn't do that.
Hell, a Platinum Square might find it tough…

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:18.040
Is something wrong?

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:20.380
Nope.

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:25.670
This kinda stuff is why I love working with young mages.

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:37.500
All things aside, I'm shocked you shattered the crystal.

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:42.170
I swear, why is it always like this with you?

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:49.250
I hear you won't have to reimburse them
for the crystal, either.

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:52.080
Yeah, thank goodness…

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:57.750
You passed, and that's all that matters.
All you have to do now is ace the written portion.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.630
R-right.

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:07.710
Speaking of, Marx, you said you had a secret weapon,
but I didn't see you use it back there.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:11.790
Yep, because it wasn't for the practical exam!

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.710
I'll be using it to its utmost potential in the written exam!

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:19.380
Behold, my incredible secret weapon!

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:20.790
Ta-da!

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:24.830
The Perfect Scorer Six-Sided Pencil!

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:29.960
This is how I got myself past Ortigia's entrance exam!

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:35.540
Well? I bet you're all wishing you had one,
but this one is mine!

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:43.130
W-well, we'll just have to give it our best shot!

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:52.960
That practical exam was harder
than I thought it would be.

00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:59.290
Like, it made me wonder if there are even people
who pass Bronze with a perfect score.

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:02.670
There aren't many perfect scorers, correct.

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:08.040
Even Platinum Squares trip up on at least something.

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:14.460
Though I believe there was one person
who got a perfect score on every exam.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:15.750
Every single one?

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:24.880
Yes. Bronze, Silver, Gold,
every exam, every question correct.

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:26.960
E-every question…

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:30.830
Why's that getting you scared?

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:34.130
You want to be a Platinum Square, right?

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:39.000
Beardy back there said you got
an easy perfect score on practical.

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:42.040
You're good at written exams, so you'll ace this one.

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:47.000
And then, what do you know,
you're right up there with that perfect scorer.

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:50.210
Vermeil…

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:54.830
She's right, you know! Don't get scared on us!

00:14:55.170 --> 00:15:00.790
But who cares about who got all perfect scores?
Just focus on this one test for now!

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:05.000
We got past the practical, let's go pass the written!

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:06.210
Yeah.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:10.630
Got it, Alto? Don't space out on this test!

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:14.420
You never know what'll trip you up on there!

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:15.710
R-right!

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:23.920
Let's go! We've got this!

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:25.830
Yeah!

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:51.130
Vermeil, the… the test is going to start soon.

00:15:51.670 --> 00:15:56.080
We've got time. There's no point
cracking open your textbook now.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:16:00.290
Besides, you used up a lot of mana back there, right?

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:05.790
I did, but… I don't need mana for the test.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:11.710
C'mon. Remember what she just said?
You never know what will trip you up.

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:20.000
Besides, I hear your heart. It wants this right now.

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:30.080
Fine. J-just a little more, all right?

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:40.960
Ugh! We're going to be cutting it close now, Vermeil!

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:44.250
Really? You still have a little time.

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:45.750
Look…

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:50.670
before you even take the exam,
you need to make sure you have your writing utensils,

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:56.880
check that you have your test ticket,
that you're sitting in the right seat, and lots more!

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:59.210
There are tons of things you need to do!

00:17:00.630 --> 00:17:04.540
I knew this before, but boy, are you a serious scholar.

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:15.540
He was that guy at the practical…

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:19.540
I hope he passes, too.

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:21.960
Hey, Alto?

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:25.790
Can I have one more?

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:27.080
No more!

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:28.630
Meanie!

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:32.790
I'm not a meanie! You know we don't have time for that!

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:40.630
Those cocky Ortigia bastards.
Bet they think they're better than us.

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:46.420
Especially that white-haired guy.
What the hell was that stunt he pulled?

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:51.040
Asshole. Just you watch. I'm gonna
blow you out of the water on the written…

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:55.630
Hey! Hi there.

00:17:56.830 --> 00:18:00.130
Uh, could you not stand there? You're in the way.

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:14.330
Sorry. It's nothing personal.

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:24.540
I'm gonna borrow your name, though.

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:47.830
Well done.

00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:54.710
You've gotten better, but you've got
a long way to go before you can beat me.

00:19:04.210 --> 00:19:06.710
Still, I'm surprised.

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:08.210
About what?

00:19:08.630 --> 00:19:14.750
About Alto Goldfield. I couldn't have imagined
he had made a demon his familiar.

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:16.710
I still can't believe it's true.

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:23.960
When I was little, I was terrified
an evil demon would steal me away.

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:32.170
And a Platinum Square might be involved, too…
the situation's getting dire.

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:36.210
You're such a worrywart, Jessica.

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:42.250
Do you truly believe she poses no threat?

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:45.580
I wonder.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:47.830
Still…

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:51.420
I think it's a splendid thing.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:56.290
Human and demon, master and familiar…

00:19:56.920 --> 00:20:05.290
If their bond is true, then it is our duty
as the Council to believe in their miracle.

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:09.830
I honestly don't quite understand.

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:14.920
Whyever would he let her give him her heart?

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:17.460
Goodness, you truly don't know?

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:21.920
He did it for love. Love!

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:26.750
He's in love with that demon.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.670
But you know something, Jessica?

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:39.580
People just call these things "miracles"...

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:42.710
...because they don't exist.

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:48.540
Goodness, it's already this late?

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:52.580
It's about time for the written exam to begin.

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:57.540
I certainly hope it concludes without incident.

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:05.580
I-I'm sorry, I got held up! Please let me in!

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:09.630
The test is about to begin. Hurry to your seat.

00:21:09.880 --> 00:21:11.250
Th-thank you!

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:17.080
Aw, man! Why can I never say no to her?!

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:24.830
Oh, Vermeil, we can't bring our familiars in
for the written test, so could you go kill time somewhere?

00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:27.210
Will do! Break a leg!

00:21:28.210 --> 00:21:29.750
Let's go, Cheryl.

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:30.420
Right.

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:32.290
Let's meet up after!

00:21:33.170 --> 00:21:33.960
Yeah!

00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:40.170
Um, I'm supposed to sit…

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:45.880
Right here! I'm so glad I made it…

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:49.790
The person sitting next to me isn't here yet?

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:51.630
Hey! You're almost late!

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:55.080
The test is about to start, get moving!

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:58.750
Gosh, that was a close one!

00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:06.960
Good luck on the test, yeah?

00:22:15.630 --> 00:22:22.580
Does it get easier with time for the immortal?

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:33.290
If I was born normal, if I become normal, can I stay close?

00:22:33.880 --> 00:22:38.710
With the children, we link our arms

00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:43.920
Make a circle and sing a song

00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:50.670
Knowing there was no chair for me all along

00:22:50.880 --> 00:22:55.960
You locked me into the dark, I'm your preserved flower

00:22:55.960 --> 00:22:59.630
The world is too slow to understand

00:22:59.630 --> 00:23:03.210
Not all blossoms spark, And spikes may be sharp

00:23:03.330 --> 00:23:07.750
They only want to see the beautiful parts

00:23:07.750 --> 00:23:11.130
Sitting in a shower of scarlet rain

00:23:11.130 --> 00:23:15.460
It all used to be ours, I'm counting the hours

00:23:15.460 --> 00:23:18.920
Hours that stood between us like a river

00:23:18.920 --> 00:23:20.920
Once I crawled through the water

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:26.460
All I ever knew have become distant past
